{%- comment -%}
  New-PDP add-on upsells — TRUE linked products.

  These cards are NOT configurator options. Each is a real Shopify
  product/variant rendering its own price and availability; clicking "Add to
  Cart" creates a SEPARATE cart line and opens the drawer (pdp-new.js). Nothing
  here touches #Product-Options-<sectionId> or hides a configurator category —
  the configurator keeps its single configured order line and this block adds
  independent ones.

  The list is a per-product metafield; unset or empty renders nothing at all.

  Accepted metafield shapes, in order of preference:

    1. list.metaobject_reference — the full shape. Each entry may define:
         variant           {Variant}  exact variant to add (authoritative)
         product           {Product}  used only when no variant is given
         default_quantity  {Integer}  quantity added per click (default 1)
         group             {Text}     tab label, e.g. "Mats"
         label             {Text}     optional card title override
       Alternate field names are accepted (quantity / tab / category) so the
       definition does not have to match one exact spelling.

       The definition also carries an admin-only `internal_name`, used as the
       metaobject's Display name so entries are identifiable in the admin
       picker. Deliberately NOT read here: naming an entry must never change
       what the customer sees.

    2. list.variant_reference — exact variants, quantity 1, single untabbed row.
    3. list.product_reference — first available variant, quantity 1, untabbed.

  Per-item quantity lives on the ENTRY, not on the upsell product, so the same
  item can add at 12 here and a different count on another machine.

  Accepts:
    - product: {Object} the PDP product (required)
    - section_id: {String} section id, for the variant-change swap target
    - heading: {String} block heading, e.g. "Add-Ons:"
    - metafield: {String} "namespace.key" of the upsell list
      (optional, default "custom.pdp_upsells")
    - block_attributes: {String} the block's shopify_attributes, so the theme
      editor can still select this block (optional)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign upsell_ns = 'custom'
  assign upsell_key = 'pdp_upsells'
  if metafield != blank
    assign mf_parts = metafield | split: '.'
    assign upsell_ns = mf_parts[0]
    if mf_parts[1] != blank
      assign upsell_key = mf_parts[1]
    endif
  endif

  assign upsell_entries = product.metafields[upsell_ns][upsell_key].value

  comment
    Tab labels, in first-appearance order. Liquid has no set type, so membership
    is tested against a delimited string — the delimiters matter, or "Mat" would
    match inside "Mats" and the second tab would be dropped.

    The accumulator carries ONE separator between neighbours (leading sep seeded,
    then label+sep per entry), so the membership probe still has a delimiter on
    both sides while split never sees an empty run. Appending the whole probe
    instead would double the separator between entries and split would yield a
    phantom "" group — a blank third tab.
  endcomment
  assign group_sep = '~|~'
  assign group_acc = group_sep
  assign ungrouped_label = 'Add-Ons'

  for entry in upsell_entries
    assign entry_group = ''
    if entry.system != blank
      assign entry_group = entry.group.value | default: entry.tab.value | default: entry.category.value
    endif
    if entry_group == blank
      assign entry_group = ungrouped_label
    endif
    assign group_probe = group_sep | append: entry_group | append: group_sep
    unless group_acc contains group_probe
      assign group_acc = group_acc | append: entry_group | append: group_sep
    endunless
  endfor

  assign upsell_groups = group_acc | remove_first: group_sep | split: group_sep
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  The wrapper id is unconditional so the variant-change swap in pdp-new.js always
  finds both a source and a target, even when the list is empty.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div id="PdpNewAddons-{{ section_id }}">
  {%- if upsell_groups.size > 0 -%}
    <div class="pdp-new__addons pdp-new__upsells" {{ block_attributes }}>
      {%- if heading != blank -%}
        <p class="pdp-new__label pdp-new__addons-heading">{{ heading | escape }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}

      <div data-tabs-section>
        {%- comment -%} A single fallback group means no labels were supplied —
            rendering one lone tab would just be a second heading. {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- unless upsell_groups.size == 1 and upsell_groups[0] == ungrouped_label -%}
          <div class="tabs__buttons pdp-new__tabs-nav">
            {%- for group in upsell_groups -%}
              <button type="button" class="tab-btn{% if forloop.first %} active{% endif %}" data-index="{{ forloop.index }}">
                {{ group | escape }}
              </button>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        {%- endunless -%}

        <div class="tabs__content pdp-new__addons-content">
          {%- for group in upsell_groups -%}
            <div class="tabs__item{% if forloop.first %} active visible{% endif %}" data-index="{{ forloop.index }}">
              <pdp-carousel class="pdp-new__addon-carousel">
                <ul class="pdp-new__addon-track" role="list">
                  {%- for entry in upsell_entries -%}
                    {%- liquid
                      comment
                        Normalise the three accepted shapes to one
                        (variant, product, quantity, group, label) tuple.
                      endcomment
                      assign up_variant = blank
                      assign up_product = blank
                      assign up_qty = 1
                      assign up_group = ''
                      assign up_label = ''

                      if entry.system != blank
                        assign up_variant = entry.variant.value
                        assign up_product = entry.product.value
                        assign up_qty = entry.default_quantity.value | default: entry.quantity.value | default: 1
                        assign up_group = entry.group.value | default: entry.tab.value | default: entry.category.value
                        assign up_label = entry.label.value
                      elsif entry.variants != blank
                        assign up_product = entry
                      else
                        assign up_variant = entry
                      endif

                      if up_variant == blank and up_product != blank
                        assign up_variant = up_product.selected_or_first_available_variant
                      endif

                      comment
                        The variant is authoritative (Tim, Aug 2): whenever one is
                        set, the card's title, image and URL come from ITS parent
                        product, never from the entry's own product field. A
                        mismatched pair would otherwise show one product while
                        adding another to the cart.
                      endcomment
                      if up_variant != blank
                        assign up_product = up_variant.product
                      endif

                      if up_group == blank
                        assign up_group = ungrouped_label
                      endif
                      if up_qty < 1
                        assign up_qty = 1
                      endif
                    -%}

                    {%- if up_group == group -%}
                    {%- comment -%} Skip an invalid, deleted or unavailable entry rather than render a
                        broken purchase path. The HTML comment is the flag: invisible to
                        customers, but it tells QA the entry was dropped deliberately. {%- endcomment -%}
                    {%- if up_variant == blank -%}
                      <!-- pdp-upsell skipped: entry has no resolvable variant (deleted or unset) -->
                    {%- elsif up_variant.available == false -%}
                      <!-- pdp-upsell skipped: {{ up_product.title | escape }} is unavailable -->
                    {%- elsif up_product.tags contains 'avisplus-product-options' -%}
                      {%- comment -%} An Avis option-holder product, not a standalone one. Adding
                          it makes a cart line that cart-drawer.liquid renders as an
                          `.extra-option-item` — a hidden sub-row of the item above it, which
                          cart-drawer.js then SUBTRACTS from the header count. The buyer sees
                          the line disappear and the count go down. {%- endcomment -%}
                      <!-- pdp-upsell skipped: {{ up_product.title | escape }} is an Avis option product (tag avisplus-product-options); point this entry at the standalone product instead -->
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- liquid
                        assign up_img = up_variant.featured_image | default: up_product.featured_image
                        assign up_title = up_label | default: up_product.title
                        assign up_line_total = up_variant.price | times: up_qty
                        comment
                          "Product Code" is the store's own metafield — the same value the
                          buy-box info tab shows. Falls back to the raw variant SKU only
                          when that field is unset.
                        endcomment
                        assign up_code = up_product.metafields.custom.product_code | default: up_variant.sku
                      -%}
                      <li class="pdp-new__addon-card">
                        <a class="pdp-new__addon-img" href="{{ up_product.url }}" tabindex="-1">
                          {%- if up_img -%}
                            <img
                              src="{{ up_img | image_url: width: 336 }}"
                              alt="{{ up_img.alt | escape }}"
                              width="168"
                              height="168"
                              loading="lazy"
                            >
                          {%- endif -%}
                        </a>
                        <div class="pdp-new__addon-info">
                          <a class="pdp-new__addon-title" href="{{ up_product.url }}">{{ up_title | escape }}</a>
                          {%- if up_code != blank -%}
                            <span class="pdp-new__addon-sku">Product Code: {{ up_code }}</span>
                          {%- endif -%}
                          <div class="pdp-new__addon-cta">
                            {%- comment -%} Unit price always, per the Figma card, plus the
                                multiple and line total when the entry adds more than one —
                                a card reading "$76.00" must not move the cart by $912.00
                                unannounced. {%- endcomment -%}
                            <span class="pdp-new__addon-price">Price: {{ up_variant.price | money }}</span>
                            {%- if up_qty > 1 -%}
                              <span class="pdp-new__addon-qty">
                                Adds {{ up_qty }} &middot; {{ up_line_total | money }} total
                              </span>
                            {%- endif -%}
                            {%- comment -%} A real, separate cart line. data-quantity carries
                                the per-item default; pdp-new.js POSTs it to /cart/add.js and
                                renders the cart drawer. {%- endcomment -%}
                            {%- comment -%} No sold-out state: an unavailable entry is
                                skipped above, so every card that renders is buyable. {%- endcomment -%}
                            <button
                              type="button"
                              class="pdp-new__addon-atc"
                              data-upsell-add
                              data-variant-id="{{ up_variant.id }}"
                              data-quantity="{{ up_qty }}"
                            >
                              {% render 'pdp-new-icon-cart', class: 'pdp-new__cart-icon--sm' %}
                              <span>Add to Cart</span>
                            </button>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      </li>
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="pdp-new__carousel-arrow pdp-new__carousel-arrow--prev"
                  aria-label="{{ 'general.slider.previous_slide' | t }}"
                  hidden
                >
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M15 6l-6 6 6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                </button>
                {%- comment -%} Both arrows start hidden; pdp-new.js reveals whichever
                    direction can actually be scrolled. Shipping `next` visible would flash
                    an arrow on groups that never need one. {%- endcomment -%}
                <button
                  type="button"
                  class="pdp-new__carousel-arrow pdp-new__carousel-arrow--next"
                  aria-label="{{ 'general.slider.next_slide' | t }}"
                  hidden
                >
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 6l6 6-6 6" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
                </button>
              </pdp-carousel>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
